# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
.angular/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Local environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Firebase — CLI artifacts and credentials
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# .firebaserc is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds only the project alias
# ("ateeqi-portfolio"), which is already public in the tracked web config and
# in every deployed URL. Ignoring it would mean anyone cloning the repo cannot
# deploy without re-running `firebase use --add`, for no security gain.

# Service-account keys and any local Angular environment file holding secrets.
# The web config in src/app/core/firebase/firebase.config.ts is NOT secret and
# is deliberately tracked; these patterns cover the ones that are.
*serviceAccount*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
src/environments/environment.local.ts
site/src/environments/environment.local.ts

# Build-time reference material — never part of the running app.
#
# Neither of these is imported, resolved or read by anything under site/: the
# only mentions are prose in code comments citing where a rule came from, and
# `angular.json`, both tsconfigs, `package.json` and `.postcssrc.json` contain
# zero references to either path. Removing them cannot affect a build.
#
# `design-reference/` is the exported Claude Design visual system (see `07`
# §0.1). It also contains a real personal photo of Muhammed, which is the
# reason it was kept out of every commit while the repository's visibility was
# undecided — ignoring it now makes that decision permanent rather than a
# habit. `10` §3 carried this as an open item and it is closed there.
#
# `.claude/skills/` holds the ui-ux-pro-max design-intelligence skill, which is
# tooling for the agent working on the repo, not a dependency of the site.
# `temp-skill/` is a second, older copy of that same skill.
#
# The skills pattern needs `**/` because the only copy lives at
# `site/.claude/`, not at the repo root. A gitignore pattern with a slash
# anywhere but the end is anchored to the directory holding the .gitignore, so
# a bare `.claude/skills/` silently matched nothing here. Scoped to `skills/`
# rather than all of `.claude/`, so a `settings.json` can still be tracked
# later if the project ever wants shared agent settings in version control.
design-reference/
**/.claude/skills/
temp-skill/
